# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Tahoe-100M perturbation model — training repository.
#
# Rule of thumb: only source code, the 3 MB drug table and the markdown docs are
# committed. Everything the server needs beyond that is either re-generated
# (models/cache) or copied over out-of-band (the h5ad data).
#
# Size reference on the dev box: data 1.0 TB, checkpoints 760 MB,
# token cache 67 MB. None of it belongs in git.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- 1. data: 593 GB + 323 GB + 85 GB -------------------------------------
data_by_plate_cell_line/
data_by_sample_embedded/
metadata/
*.h5ad
*.h5
*.loom
*.zarr/

# --- 2. runtime artifacts --------------------------------------------------
# checkpoints (models/runs/<name>/{last,best}.pt ~380 MB each), TensorBoard
# event files, csv logs, and the MolFormer token cache (67 MB, rebuild with
# `python models/molformer_atoms.py`)
models/runs/
models/runtime/
models/cache/
*.pt
*.pth
*.ckpt
*.safetensors
events.out.tfevents.*

# --- 3. generated analysis output -----------------------------------------
# the .md reports are kept (they document the gradient study); the binary and
# machine-dumped artefacts next to them are not needed to train
models/testing/*.png
models/testing/*.json
models/testing/*.txt
models/testing/*.log
dataset_size_comparison.png

# --- 4. python / editor / OS ----------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.venv/
venv/
env/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# --- 5. not needed to train (left on the dev box, not shipped) -------------
# uncomment any of these if you decide to version them
Analysis/
docs/
utils/
tests/
logs/
groups.json
*.ipynb

# keep the notebook the model was ported from: it is the reference implementation
!models/modelr.ipynb
